    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="1002" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg972"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/8–147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Troutman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-01T18:00:00+01:00">August 1, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>800. For Lovett and Nitze from Clayton. Absolutely essential I have authority act
                    wool tariff tomorrow morning as fear cannot hold Dominion Cabinet members here
                    longer. Have been trying telephone you all day to urge Secretary himself go to
                    President this afternoon, but line out of order. Am still trying to phone.
                    [Clayton.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Troutman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
